From: Anton <fourth@devpins.org>
Subject: drm/panel: port the fork's panels to the v7.2 drm_panel alloc API

The sdm845-mainline device delta (patch 0001) was written against the
pre-v7.2 drm_panel API. In v7.2 drm_panel_init() is no longer exported --
it is static in drivers/gpu/drm/drm_panel.c and only reachable through
__devm_drm_panel_alloc(), i.e. panels must be allocated with the
devm_drm_panel_alloc(dev, type, member, funcs, connector_type) macro,
which allocates the container, initialises the embedded drm_panel and
takes the initial refcount. Three of the fork's panel drivers still call
drm_panel_init() and fail to build:

  drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw49410-lh609qh1.c:472: error: call to
    undeclared function 'drm_panel_init'
  drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt35596s.c:479: error: call to
    undeclared function 'drm_panel_init'
  drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-ea8076.c:217: (same, the build stops
    at the first two)

sw49410 already allocates with devm_drm_panel_alloc() and merely kept a
leftover drm_panel_init() call, so the call is simply dropped. nt35596s
and ea8076 are converted from devm_kzalloc() to devm_drm_panel_alloc();
the funcs/connector-type arguments move from the removed init call into
the allocation, so behaviour is unchanged.

Also silence

  drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43408.c:62:12: warning: unused function
    'sw43408_unprepare'

which the fork introduces on purpose: 0001 splits sw43408's power-down
into ->disable and ->unprepare but leaves `.unprepare` commented out in
sw43408_funcs (the panel is not powered down on the OnePlus 6). Keep the
helper and its intent, mark it __maybe_unused.

None of these panels are used by beryllium (the Poco F1 uses
novatek-nt36672a / ebbg-ft8719), but they are built =y by the config, so
they must compile.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43408.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43408.c
@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@
